{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 214 days before the posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D14"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the furosemide injection shortage on 2020-04-07 and it remains current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E69", "E60"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Accord Healthcare product used at Corvale East and Corvale Lakeside is labeled with Intas Pharmaceuticals Limited as the manufacturing plant.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E7", "E18"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspected Intas Pharmaceuticals Limited (FEI 3004011473) and classified the inspection OAI on 2019-09-06, which was 214 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D14", "E14"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA later issued an OAI classification letter to Intas Pharmaceuticals Limited dated 2023-04-05, and an import alert 66-40 was published on 2023-06-01 for the same firm.",
      "cites": ["D18", "E16"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Hospira product used at Corvale General is labeled with Pfizer Healthcare India Private Limited as a manufacturing plant.",
      "cites": ["E5", "E59"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspected Pfizer Healthcare India Private Limited (FEI 3008316085) and classified the inspection OAI on 2019-09-06, with the classification letter dated 2020-05-25, 48 days after the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["D14", "D19", "E56"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule-based best option is to transfer 33 vials of 10 mg/mL, 2 mL from Corvale Lakeside to Corvale East, which would raise Corvale East from 8.5 days to 12 days on hand while Corvale Lakeside retains two weeks of supply.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D3", "D21"]
    }
  ]
}
